  "scope": "Three fixed implementation discriminators; no larger census, asymptotic fit, or new query identity. Canonical concatenation/splitting preserve the exact generator word.",
  "proof": "Induct on word length. A canonical root split is unique. The concat/split cases divide only into shorter words, preserve chronological order, and intern precisely that unique split. Thus all parenthesizations of an equal generator word return the same node. The inherited exact section identities and contextual normalizer remain valid.",
